---
import VIShell from '../../components/VIShell.astro';
import ClampFace from '../../components/vi/ClampFace.astro';
import ClampPanels from '../../components/vi/ClampPanels.astro';
import { u } from '../../utils/url';
---

<VIShell
  slug="dcm-5410-tr" model="DCM 5410 TR"
  pageTitle="DCM 5410 TR Playground: AC/DC Clamp Meter Online"
  description="Just for fun: a free interactive playground version of the CIE DCM 5410 TR AC/DC clamp multimeter: 1000 A AC and DC, frequency, capacitance and temperature. Clamp a solar string, zero the DC offset, capture motor inrush."
  h1="DCM 5410 TR, in your browser"
  intro="The AC and DC clamp. Zero the DC offset, clamp a solar string, capture a motor's starting surge, then check frequency, duty cycle, capacitance and temperature with the same meter."
  productHref={u('/products/clamp-meters/dcm-5410-tr/')}
  extraLink={{ href: u('/tools/three-phase-power-calculator/'), label: 'Three-phase power calculator' }}
  ctaBody="The DCM 5410 TR is supplied by CIE in Howrah, with test certificate available on request."
>
  <Fragment slot="stage"><ClampFace model="5410" /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="hint">Turn the dial, click the left trigger to open or close the jaw. Keys: <kbd>↑</kbd> <kbd>↓</kbd> dial, <kbd>J</kbd> jaw, <kbd>S</kbd> SELECT, <kbd>H</kbd> HOLD, <kbd>B</kbd> backlight, <kbd>Z</kbd> ZERO.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="panels"><ClampPanels model="5410" /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="about">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AC and DC current:</strong> on the 60 A and 600/1000 A positions the orange SELECT button switches between AC (True-RMS) and DC. DC current uses a Hall-effect sensor, which has an offset. Open the jaw (or clamp nothing) and press <strong>ZERO</strong> before every DC reading.</li>
      <li><strong>Inrush (INR):</strong> on an AC current range, hold ZERO/INR for two seconds to enter inrush mode, then start the motor. The meter shows the True-RMS value of the maximum current in the first 200 ms, typically several times the running current.</li>
      <li><strong>REL:</strong> press REL to store the present reading as a reference. After that the display shows the difference. Hold it down for the torch.</li>
      <li><strong>Frequency and duty:</strong> the Hz% position measures from 10 Hz to 10 MHz; SELECT toggles frequency and duty cycle, useful for PWM and inverter outputs.</li>
      <li><strong>Capacitance and temperature:</strong> the Ω position also covers continuity, diode test and capacitance (1 nF to 10 mF). The °C °F position reads a K-type thermocouple; the display range is -20 °C to 1000 °C, and the supplied probe is rated to 250 °C. Discharge capacitors before testing.</li>
      <li><strong>Ghost voltage, NCV:</strong> Low-Z mode ignores ghost voltage. The NCV position senses the field around live conductors.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="vi-fine">This is a training simulation. Ranges and functions come from the DCM 5410 TR specification. Button behaviour and the continuity buzzer threshold (50 Ω) follow the instruction manual; the display layout is approximated, and the low-pass filter (V.F.C) voltage mode, the high-voltage warning and the Live-wire probe test are not simulated. Always follow the instruction manual, use the correct CAT-rated leads and treat every circuit as live until proved dead.</p>
  </Fragment>
</VIShell>

<script is:inline src="/js/vi-core.js"></script>
<script is:inline>window.CLAMP_MODEL = '5410';</script>
<script is:inline src="/js/vi-clamp.js"></script>
